# Test hints for RecursiveActions
# Covers ARO-0081 §9: nested-frame recursion (Factorial), tail-call
# recursion that reuses its frame (SumTo, 10 000 deep), and mutual
# recursion (IsEven/IsOdd). Runs in both interpreted and compiled mode;
# compiled mode nests every frame, so the compiled run is the slow one.
type: console

# 180s, not the default 60 (GitLab #654's pipeline run, and main's own).
#
# `SumTo` is 10 000 deep, and compiled mode nests every frame even for a tail
# call — so the compiled run is 10 000 live frames however the source is
# written. That is the point of the example, and it is also genuinely slow:
# ~2.6s on an idle laptop, ~45-60s on a shared CI runner with several
# pipelines competing for it. It crossed the 60s default intermittently and
# took `main` red, which blocks every merge.
#
# The depth is what ARO-0081 §9 is demonstrating, so the budget moves rather
# than the example.
timeout: 180
